{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory handled the main pediatric pneumonia safety chain well: it checked current respiratory status, prioritized red flags, set medication boundaries, and routed result interpretation to the ward team. However, RC6 was authored as a required responsibility-chain item and the visible trajectory did not address the privacy/contact-history/external-record sharing barrier despite the fragmented outside-film/result context being visible, so this is a minor/moderate in-chain omission. Under the frozen rubric, any minor/moderate responsibility-chain error caps the grade at 2 even though the doctor completed meaningful higher-order clarification of hidden result/medication facts and corrected case-specific misconceptions.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00122",
        "explanation": "The doctor left a safe, executable open plan tied to inpatient reassessment and further review rather than claiming the episode was fully resolved.",
        "quote": "下午医生复评后，把衣原体检测类型、用药是否调整及影像范围告诉我"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00137",
        "explanation": "The caregiver later demonstrated receipt of the inpatient plan and medication boundary.",
        "quote": "药和雾化不要我们自己停、自己加、自己改"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The observable doctor closure was best characterized as a safe open handoff: the caregiver had concrete red flags, medication boundaries, and inpatient follow-up tasks, while remaining questions were to be handled by the ward team. The final caregiver message was not answered, but it largely confirmed the same safe plan already given.",
